    "narrative": {
        "northStar": "The Key Store in Daylight",
        "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Key Store in Daylight\"**\n\nThe storefront is a bright, well-signed key store: a white floor with navy print, turquoise signage that frames the shop (the header with its menu bar, the banner slider, the benefits band and the footer), and one warm coral that says \"do this\" (the primary action, the cart count, the current menu item, prices on stickers). Everything else is quiet: soft blue-grey panels, hairline borders, and the game covers carrying the color.\n\nDensity is that of a working key store: one strict grid of product cards, each with its cover on top, the title, type and region, where it is activated, and the price with \"Agregar\" at the foot. Every cover wears its platform's retail band, so a listing reads as PS5, Xbox, Switch or Steam at a glance. Real cover art comes from IGDB; when a product has none, the system prints a typographic cover on a deep tint. Motion is soft and physical: covers tilt toward the pointer, buttons press to 0.97, lists rise in with a short stagger, and everything falls back to opacity and color under `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n\nTokens are named by role (`bg`, `surface`, `fg`, `brand`, `accent`…), not by value. A future dark theme only redefines their values under `:root[data-theme='dark']`; the turquoise sections already use this mechanism through `.surface-brand`. Two old materials survive where they still do a job: the thermal receipt for money summaries and the whiteboard sign on the error page.",
        "keyCharacteristics": [
            "White ground, navy text; turquoise brand sections at the top and bottom of the page.",
            "Coral marks the one primary action, the cart and the current menu item; text on it is dark.",
            "Every cover carries an official platform band; PC games show the store where they are activated.",
            "Condensed extra-bold caps for headings, buttons, prices and covers; Rubik for reading.",
            "Thermal paper and monospace for every money summary.",
            "Colors only through role tokens; a test rejects raw colors."
        ],
        "rules": [
            {
                "name": "The Role Token Rule",
                "body": "Components use role tokens only; `test/unit/design-tokens.test.ts` fails on hex, `rgb()`, arbitrary color classes and color utilities without a token in `@theme`. A new color is a new role in `main.css`, never a value in a `.vue` file.",
                "section": "colors"
            },
            {
                "name": "The Brand Surface Rule",
                "body": "Inside a turquoise section, wrap it in `.surface-brand` and keep using `bg`, `fg`, `line`, `brand`: the class redefines them (white text, translucent white surfaces and lines, `brand` turns white). Never hand-pick white-on-turquoise utilities.",
                "section": "colors"
            },
            {
                "name": "The One Coral Rule",
                "body": "Coral fills the single primary action of a view, prices on stickers, the cart count and the current menu item. A second coral button on the same screen means one of them is secondary.",
                "section": "colors"
            },
            {
                "name": "The Material Rule",
                "body": "Paper belongs to receipts, the board to the error sign, cover tints and platform bands to covers.",
                "section": "colors"
            },
            {
                "name": "The Tabular Price Rule",
                "body": "Every price, count, countdown and reference uses tabular figures (`data`, `time` and `.tabular` get them by default) and comes from the API in CLP.",
                "section": "typography"
            },
            {
                "name": "The Marker Stays on the Sign Rule",
                "body": "Permanent Marker appears only on the error page's whiteboard sign.",
                "section": "typography"
            },
            {
                "name": "The Shadow Follows the Object Rule",
                "body": "Shadows belong to covers, stickers, buttons and receipts. Panels, bands, nav bars and form sections have borders or tonal steps, not shadows.",
                "section": "elevation"
            }
        ],
        "dos": [
            "**Do** keep the page on White Floor (#ffffff) with Navy Ink text, and put turquoise only on the brand sections (header, menu bar, banner, benefits, footer).",
            "**Do** wrap every turquoise section in `.surface-brand` and keep using role tokens inside it.",
            "**Do** add new colors as role tokens in `app/assets/css/main.css`; a future dark theme redefines values under `:root[data-theme='dark']`.",
            "**Do** put every price in display 800 with tabular figures, in CLP from the API.",
            "**Do** give every cover its platform band, and show the activation store (not \"PC\") for PC and Mac games.",
            "**Do** print every money summary (cart, checkout, result, order) on the thermal receipt in JetBrains Mono.",
            "**Do** give pressable elements the 0.97 press and reduce all motion to opacity and color under `prefers-reduced-motion`."
        ],
        "donts": [
            "**Don't** write raw colors (hex, `rgb()`, `bg-[#…]`) in `.vue` files, or color utilities without a token; the design-tokens test fails.",
            "**Don't** use more than one coral action per view, or white text on coral.",
            "**Don't** add a frame around cover art; the band is the only mark.",
            "**Don't** put station numbers or price stickers on listing cards.",
            "**Don't** use Permanent Marker outside the error sign, or paper and board colors outside their objects.",
            "**Don't** show \"before\" prices, invented discounts, ratings or reviews.",
            "**Don't** put shadows on panels, bands, nav bars or form sections; use borders and tonal steps."
        ]
    }
}
